12. Exact visual layering and glassmorphism implementation
One of the most important aspects of recreating this design is understanding how the layers interact.

The glass effect is not simply background: rgba(255,255,255,.1).

The reference has multiple layers of depth.
12.1 Layer stack
The correct rendering order should be:
Layer 1 — Base environment

Full-screen photographic nighttime background

Layer 2 — Environmental overlays

Dark gradients, vignette, blue atmospheric haze

Layer 3 — Decorative visuals

Earth, stars, lighting and background effects

Layer 4 — Glass surfaces

Translucent navy surfaces with backdrop blur

Layer 5 — Component borders and illumination

Cyan edges, green reflections and soft shadows

Layer 6 — UI content

Typography, icons, charts, buttons and indicators


12.2 Glass surface transparency
Different components should have different transparency levels.
Component	Suggested background opacity
Navigation	40–50%
Farm selector	70–78%
Main conditions panel	68–75%
Field cards	78–86%
Alert cards	82–90%
Weather panel	72–82%
Bottom status panel	72–82%

These are starting implementation values, not measured alpha-channel values from the original image.
12.3 Border treatment
Avoid generic bright white borders.

The design uses colored borders with low opacity.

Recommended:
/* Blue glass */
border: 1px solid rgba(64, 182, 241, 0.34);

/* Cyan illuminated glass */
border: 1px solid rgba(46, 206, 246, 0.48);

/* Green success glass */
border: 1px solid rgba(38, 239, 166, 0.40);


12.4 Backdrop blur
Suggested values:
Element	Blur
Navigation	18 px
Farm selector	16 px
Main panel	17–20 px
Field cards	12–15 px
Weather panel	18 px
Bottom panel	20 px

Do not over-blur the background. It must remain identifiable through the panels.
12.5 Glow intensity
There are three different glow types:

Ambient glow: large, soft, low-opacity lighting surrounding the panel.

Edge glow: thin luminous light around the panel's outline.

Accent glow: concentrated green or cyan illumination around individual icons and controls.

Keep the ambient glow relatively subtle. The strongest glow belongs to the main Farm Conditions border, health ring, primary button, and bottom green status illustration.

