17. Animation and interaction details
The original appearance is relatively calm. It should not be turned into an excessively animated gaming interface.

Animations should be smooth, subtle, and purposeful.
Element	Animation	Suggested duration
Health ring	Animated progress draw	1.5 s
Active navigation	Green glow transition	250 ms
Primary button	Slight brightness increase on hover	200 ms
Field cards	Slight upward movement on hover	200 ms
Main panel	Subtle border illumination	3 s
Live indicator	Soft green pulse	2 s
Earth	Extremely slow atmospheric movement	15–25 s
Background	Optional subtle parallax	Continuous
Refresh icon	Rotation on refresh	600 ms

Example:

@keyframes livePulse {
  0%, 100% {
    box-shadow: 0 0 4px rgba(0,255,153,.25);
    opacity: 1;
  }

  50% {
    box-shadow: 0 0 12px rgba(0,255,153,.65);
    opacity: .8;
  }
}

.live-dot {
  animation: livePulse 2s ease-in-out infinite;
}

.field-card {
  transition:
    transform .2s ease,
    border-color .2s ease,
    box-shadow .2s ease;
}

.field-card:hover {
  transform: translateY(-2px);

  border-color:
    rgba(43, 231, 220, .55);

  box-shadow:
    0 0 17px rgba(0, 193, 225, .18);
}

.primary-button {
  transition:
    filter .2s ease,
    transform .2s ease;
}

.primary-button:hover {
  filter: brightness(1.1);
  transform: translateY(-1px);
}



Respect prefers-reduced-motion so that users who disable animations are not forced to see them.

